WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.044
"Reversing Early-Stage Prostate Cancer Progression
with a Plant-Based Diet and Lifestyle Program"

00:00:07.215 --> 00:00:09.840
Higher consumption of
a healthy plant-based diet

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.240
was significantly associated
with a lower chance

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.240
of having an elevated PSA,

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.480
which can be a sign
of prostate cancer.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.400
We're talking about
potentially cutting the odds

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.920
of having an elevated PSA
in half with diet.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.160
The researchers concluded:
"This study provides

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.000
strong evidence
supporting the potential use

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.760
of plant-based foods
in the prevention

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.480
and treatment
of prostate cancer."

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.520
"Not so fast", replied
an editor of the journal,

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.320
"This paper certainly
doesn't present final,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.480
convincing proof
that reduced PSA levels

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.960
due to a plant-based diet
in fact translate

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.480
into what we actually care
about: less prostate cancer."

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.040
Harvard cohort researchers
took up the mantle

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.320
to answer that question.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:49.680
And indeed,
greater consumption

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.320
of a healthful
plant-based diet does appear

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.560
to reduce the risk
of getting prostate cancer

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.480
and dying from prostate cancer

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.080
by nearly half
for men under age 65.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.520
And those adhering more to a healthy
plant-based diet who do get cancer

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:04.800
had 90 percent lower odds

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.920
of ending up with high-grade,
more severe prostate cancer

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.960
and appeared to be better able
to handle cancer treatment

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.520
and ended up with
better sexual function,

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.720
less incontinence,
and more vitality.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.960
This is consistent with the role
of diet and nutrition

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.280
in the prevention and treatment
of cancer more generally,

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.120
where the evidence points
to a diet

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.520
with minimal animal products.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.040
What if you already
have cancer though?

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.760
Study findings suggest that
adhering to plant-based diets

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.560
may be beneficial
for overall cancer survival

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.360
and may potentially improve
the prognosis for common cancers

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:40.960
such as breast, colorectal,
and prostate cancers.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:44.080
It starts with
case reports like this.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.000
A 73-year-old man
with prostate cancer

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.360
was placed
on a plant-based diet,

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.120
and within 10 days,

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.960
his tumor markers were down
about 75 percent.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:56.240
But case reports
are like glorified anecdotes.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.160
You can't know
if a healthier diet

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.520
and lifestyle actually help

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.240
until you run a randomized,
controlled trial

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:05.120
and put it to the test.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:07.840
Dr. Dean Ornish,
famous for showing

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.960
the progression of heart disease
could be reversed,

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.480
opening up arteries
without drugs,

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.320
without surgery,
just a plant-based diet

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.840
and lifestyle program,
eliminating angina chest pain

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.600
in about three-quarters
of patients

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.440
within a matter of months.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:24.640
He decided to move
from killer #1— heart disease—

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.880
to killer #2—cancer.

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:31.120
93 men with early-stage
watch-and-wait prostate cancer

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.960
were randomized
to either standard care

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:37.680
or a plant-based diet along
with walking and relaxation.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.480
The cancer tended to get worse
in the control group

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:43.840
but comparatively better
in the plant-based group.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.960
When blood from the patients
on the standard diet

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:50.720
was dripped onto prostate cancer
cells growing in a petri dish,

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:54.560
cancer cell growth rates
were cut by 9 percent.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.400
Their bodies were doing the best
they could to beat back the cancer.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.920
The blood of patients on the
plant-based program, though,

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.680
knocked down the cancer
growth by 70 percent.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.120
Eating and living
more healthfully

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:12.480
made their blood stream almost eight
times less hospitable to cancer.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.400
Now, this was after a year.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.240
Subsequent studies
have shown that you can see

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:18.400
a significant
cancer-fighting effect

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.240
after less than two weeks

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:24.480
on a similar Pritikin-style
plant-based diet with exercise.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:27.280
Ornish took biopsies from
the prostate cancer patients

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:30.480
before and after three months
and saw a significant change

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.600
in the expression
of more than 500 genes.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.080
You can see the subtle shift
in gene regulation

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:38.160
from more red to more green.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.120
The green denotes genes
that are being downregulated

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.640
under the lifestyle changes,
before and after.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.320
Of course,
what we really care about

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.000
are disease outcomes.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.640
By the two-year follow-up,
significantly more men

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.600
in the control group
had enough cancer progression

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.160
that they had to go
into treatment, for example,

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.720
five had to get
radical prostatectomies,

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.880
which can lead
to urinary incontinence

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:03.600
and impotence in 60 percent,

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.160
whereas none of the men
in the lifestyle group

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:08.400
were forced to go into surgery.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.680
What about those
with more serious disease?

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.440
Researchers followed 10 patients
with recurrent prostate cancer,

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.480
meaning those whose
invasive cancer had to be cut

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.080
or burned out with radiation,

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:23.040
yet their PSA levels
started to rise again,

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:25.760
signaling the cancer was back.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:28.400
There was no control group
per se in this study.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.480
Each patient was
kind of their own control

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.560
before and after,
being asked to center

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:35.360
their diets around
more whole plant foods.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:38.960
There was a significant decrease
in the rate of PSA rise,

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.920
suggesting a slowing
of cancer growth.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:43.840
4 out of 10 patients

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:46.000
actually saw their PSA levels
go down,

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.120
suggesting the possibility

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.640
of at least some degree
of disease remission.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:54.800
9 out of 10 had a reduction
in their rates of PSA rise

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:58.160
as well as an improvement
of their PSA doubling times,

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:03.200
which is a proxy for how fast
the tumor doubles in size.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.440
The increase
in average doubling time

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:08.560
went from about 12 months
before the dietary change

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:11.440
to 112 months,

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:14.560
which is the largest that has
ever been reported in any kind

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:18.400
of dietary intervention trial
for recurrent prostate cancer.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.480
What about
really advanced cancer,

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.040
stage four with spread
to distant organs?

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.800
Out of nine patients
willing to go on

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.960
a plant-based
macrobiotic diet,

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.520
three men experienced
long-term regression

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.760
of multiple
bone lesions,

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.520
compared to no regression
or healing

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.440
in nine matched
control subjects

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:38.560
who continued eating
the standard American diet.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:40.160
Those on the healthier diet

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:43.280
went on to live
an average of 19 years more,

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.520
compared to those with
the same severity of cancer

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:48.960
not even living
for 4 years more, on average,

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:50.640
on their standard diet.

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:53.440
Now this was not
a randomized study,

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:54.880
so maybe it says something

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:57.040
about those
willing to eat healthfully

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.440
rather than
healthful eating itself.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:01.440
But what's the downside?

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.960
As Dr. Ornish likes to say,

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:06.400
"The only side effects
are good ones."

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:07.600
A large number of patients

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.920
with metastatic prostate cancer,
for example,

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.400
die not from their cancer,

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.800
but rather
from non-cancer causes,

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.280
and the number one cause
is heart disease,

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:22.448
so, a heart-healthy diet
could only help.

